#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092033 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "7302747a-df6d-5aa9-8118-c9e5f3b1574d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6192" :question/problem "Calculate, in degrees to the nearest degree, the solutions to the equation $5\\sin x = -7\\cos x$ for $0^\\circ \\leq x < 360^\\circ.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide each term of the equation by $\\cos x$ and use the identity $\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-\\frac{7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-\\frac{7\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ 5\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-7 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\tan x = -\\dfrac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nThe length of the interval for $x$ is $2\\pi$, so we will likely require $2$ solutions. \n\nWe can immediately calculate the principal value $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan\\left(-\\dfrac{7}{5}\\right) \\approx -54.46\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the domain $0^\\circ \\leq x < 360^\\circ.$ To get a value that's inside the domain, we add $180^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{7}{5})+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈-{54.46}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={125.54}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the other solution inside the given interval, we add $180^\\circ$ to $x_1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{125.54}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={305.54}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solutions, rounded to the nearest degree, are $x= 126^\\circ, 306^\\circ.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092034 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "072d7328-7c31-5d09-b2d3-91b564624b62" :question/math-academy-id "e-6196" :question/problem "Calculate, in degrees to the nearest degree, the solutions to the equation $3\\sin x + 12\\cos x = 0$ for $-180^\\circ <  x \\leq 180^\\circ.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide each term of the equation by $\\cos x$ and use the identity $\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{12\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+12 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-12 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can immediately calculate the principal value $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan(-4) \\approx -75.96^\\circ\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the given domain, our first solution is $x_1 = -75.96^\\circ.$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we *add* $180^\\circ.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈-{75.96}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={104.04}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solutions, rounded to the nearest degree, are $x= -76^\\circ, 104^\\circ.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a693634-7d7f-58c5-8543-c96b389bafc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334415} {:answer/id #uuid "f4079bc1-b3b2-5fcd-8b9b-0083c0657ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,010" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334416} {:answer/id #uuid "871b6304-0373-5c38-9be8-3ff814595391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\,892" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334417} {:answer/id #uuid "4d8cfb00-f8ac-5efe-9911-f1f11307c39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,487" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334418} {:answer/id #uuid "72e352ed-257b-5929-b793-ff50dc14a93f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4079bc1-b3b2-5fcd-8b9b-0083c0657ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,010" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334416} :answer-field/id #uuid "fac15273-df87-5b5f-9bf3-c8a54ae6ab93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "522c4c61-4495-5931-943a-362bbbc1e1b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122673" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest degree?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{6\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)≈{80.538}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${80.538}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={80.538}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract ${180}^{∘}$ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={80.538}^{∘}-{180}^{∘}≈-{99.462}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $80.538\\cdot (-99.462)≈-8\\,010.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c041f9-f522-5183-8cb6-12c9d870ca9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36{\\pi }^{2}}{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334422} {:answer/id #uuid "275f56c1-863b-5026-818c-b03125703d6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36\\pi }{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334423} {:answer/id #uuid "032c15da-959d-52f5-890e-f2996d46c640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334424} {:answer/id #uuid "43063b8f-df7a-5448-bd10-557e9bf7caf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55\\pi }{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334425} {:answer/id #uuid "9dcd4c97-841c-5b1e-a5e1-7e6abe840952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dcd4c97-841c-5b1e-a5e1-7e6abe840952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334426} :answer-field/id #uuid "614c4d4a-9018-525c-aeea-a4954c1ee8f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e1c09e9-6554-5dcd-aed9-01c917440de8" :question/math-academy-id "q-21607" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=x+2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{11\\pi }{6}=\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e50b34f9-5701-5bf0-a0e7-ec62466b033f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334429} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe28804-38f4-522d-90c7-24d692d732f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e50b34f9-5701-5bf0-a0e7-ec62466b033f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334429} :answer-field/id #uuid "096f627c-e501-5c9d-9a75-2be8b4af0785" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1b9744-6b9a-5188-ae4f-1bb29558b8f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f1b9744-6b9a-5188-ae4f-1bb29558b8f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334432} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d4ae52-db0c-526c-becd-d99f8063bc25" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f92d416-4a19-5cd0-a0f1-8a1e9373ff75" :question/math-academy-id "q-330495" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{8}{3})≈1.212\\,03\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\nx≈1.212\\,03+\\pi ≈4.353\\,62\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.21,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d607832-040d-5837-bd6e-91fc0461dea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334435} {:answer/id #uuid "02501101-4df0-5fff-a801-7fff985f15e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02501101-4df0-5fff-a801-7fff985f15e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334436} :answer-field/id #uuid "226e297d-0a17-5b36-8add-b9e44a46837b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334434} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "580a6509-097c-5f64-a4c9-eb13d6530e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "580a6509-097c-5f64-a4c9-eb13d6530e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334438} :answer-field/id #uuid "2131e877-88eb-5c75-b22d-a76d1b1e5f71" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "391ef030-a808-5483-bfcf-8d5d0b810584" :question/math-academy-id "q-330590" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =5 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})≈1.190\\,29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find another solution in the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi )$, we subtract $\\pi :$\n\n$$\nx≈1.190\\,29-\\pi ≈-1.951\\,30\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈-1.95,\\,{x}_{2}≈1.19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f60a395-ae1b-5285-b8fd-906c4071aca1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334441} {:answer/id #uuid "8b89faa9-2317-568a-810c-cb1e53ab6b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f60a395-ae1b-5285-b8fd-906c4071aca1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334441} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3b6134-c475-52df-b845-3d1464ae3eed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334440} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e209f8c9-f0ff-59af-8985-82cbc1fb9b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e209f8c9-f0ff-59af-8985-82cbc1fb9b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334444} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e44de73-c556-5076-bacb-a8cb1d572acd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "247fbd34-ae4e-58c1-818b-930fa4d84a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-330627" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide each term of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{7\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{2})≈1.292\\,50\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}≈1.292\\,50+\\pi ≈4.434\\,09\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.29,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.43.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a68f6b0-26ed-50d7-bf3c-758b5196d3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334447} {:answer/id #uuid "0c63f889-7581-5098-a6a9-cc5232925bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.306" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334448} {:answer/id #uuid "0b87879d-ac03-5c2d-a111-c9bc0373e900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.062" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334449} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc5c472-d6e8-5e40-a41a-6bb6e2d031e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334450} {:answer/id #uuid "fec7db22-9de3-505e-a0c1-ad866b25b37e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fec7db22-9de3-505e-a0c1-ad866b25b37e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334451} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb088d7-ab70-51b0-b357-1cedba672feb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f8bfbe2-b922-56e7-8c09-11a1f10461da" :question/math-academy-id "q-8831" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-5 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})=1.190\\,289\\,949…≈1.190\\,290\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $1.190\\,290$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.190\\,290.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +1.190\\,289\\,949…=4.331\\,882\\,603\\,…≈4.331\\,883\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.190\\,290\\cdot 4.331\\,883≈5.156\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0d74397-059d-5b48-aec2-fd64b98c973a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.685" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334454} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb0e5ba-bf3e-5a6b-ae7f-2ebba218c67c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.850" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334455} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef69f4a-85d2-5742-864e-c7d9d1f905e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.859" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334456} {:answer/id #uuid "9627af9e-888f-5c62-9ef9-e1b8a9220cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.860" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334457} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fb9a89-045a-5424-a6c4-246853f976de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9627af9e-888f-5c62-9ef9-e1b8a9220cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.860" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334457} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaaf9440-6975-54a0-b0b7-458421040865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "457eab8b-55e1-586d-b37d-d7583b92f4b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-8835" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{4}{3})=-0.927\\,295\\,218…≈-0.927\\,295\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to 6 decimal places. \n\nSince $-0.927\\,295$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=-0.927\\,295…+\\pi ≈2.214\\,297 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=-0.927\\,295…+2\\pi ≈5.355\\,890\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈2.214\\,297\\cdot 5.355\\,890≈11.860\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d2892c1-8988-5b1e-b341-ab4a1fa46866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.787" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334461} {:answer/id #uuid "beafe223-41aa-5a15-8822-699b56b7d26a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.407" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334462} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2d6613-073e-5e81-b5a3-223e6c163096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.367" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334463} {:answer/id #uuid "7f214933-2cc3-58ac-b522-713ec221fbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.499" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334464} {:answer/id #uuid "93fd7450-b01c-59be-89a6-bd562e182cb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.157" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beafe223-41aa-5a15-8822-699b56b7d26a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.407" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334462} :answer-field/id #uuid "675a29db-136d-52db-9f80-5562f0f8c1f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ded74ca-6dcb-53b6-9e83-9f98736a964d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8870" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{16\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-16 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =16 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4)=1.325\\,817\\,663…≈1.325\\,818\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $1.325\\,818$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.325\\,818.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=1.325\\,817\\,663…-\\pi =-1.815\\,774\\,989…≈-1.815\\,775\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.325\\,818\\cdot (-1.815\\,775)≈-2.407\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba1bb589-53b5-5c64-82e5-e9ea1b169814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334468} {:answer/id #uuid "6f7b93e0-98cf-5be2-8a42-0aacddac3112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334469} {:answer/id #uuid "8046f224-b274-5617-a4d0-eac096290dcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334470} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3b9567-4608-56b3-9335-8ff92260b844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334471} {:answer/id #uuid "31019fc4-6c7f-5dc2-84bd-3f7452a605b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5.86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f7b93e0-98cf-5be2-8a42-0aacddac3112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334469} :answer-field/id #uuid "67fd613a-0346-5af5-a6d2-ac898103d555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14075095-b35c-5376-9922-d351dd7229a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-8873" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-0.463\\,647…≈-0.463\\,65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSince $-0.463\\,65$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.463\\,65.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-0.463\\,65…+\\pi ≈2.677\\,95\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈-0.463\\,65\\cdot 2.677\\,95≈-1.24\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b0272d-8eed-5f4d-b5b3-6b329d4f575e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7π^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091476} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fa19fe-6805-57f3-af01-4fbf8dc1db3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{π^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091477} {:answer/id #uuid "1b92f980-c7d4-5710-b20b-64f9b024e034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5π^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091478} {:answer/id #uuid "224e62b7-54d3-5eff-a1e4-4c606e1e5a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{π^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091479} {:answer/id #uuid "7c60c279-ff47-5a7c-8817-eea4376bf832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{π^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b92f980-c7d4-5710-b20b-64f9b024e034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5π^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091478} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b307dce-83c1-5dc6-b94a-9680cbb09d46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40bdf0c4-a9af-5a19-bf92-60c84db76070" :question/math-academy-id "q-8876" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}=-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$"}]}
